From 95c9d88c30088aaa01999ffb609c2f111071c6f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:17:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] device: touch-driven scroll detection for the E-Ink scroll
 mode

Chrome, WebView and Flutter scroll without accessibility scroll events,
so the per-app scroll optimization (fast waveform while scrolling) never
engaged there. While the foreground app opts into scroll optimization,
the E-Ink service holds an input gesture monitor (a spy: events still
reach the app, pointers are never pilfered). Finger drags beyond 10 px
(the stock threshold) feed the existing scroll path and settle table;
stylus and mouse input are ignored, and accessibility scroll events keep
working as before. Kill switch: persist.debug.hibreak.touch_scroll=false
(applied at the next app switch).

A drag over the keyguard or the notification shade, or with the screen off, does not toggle scroll mode (checked once per drag: interactive, keyguard not locked, no active or focused SystemUI system window; the service now retrieves the interactive windows list). No log per drag.
---
